/// Balances at the start of March, from the bank apps and the wallet, and what the collective's account held.
opening 2025-03-01
  checking            5_218.44 USD
  savings             3_100.00 USD
  wallet                240.00 USD
  collective-checking 1_842.30 USD
  collective-cash        96.50 USD
  visa                  412.66 USD

/// Rent is 3,150.00 USD for the flat, paid by me from checking. My third is the rent; Ben's and Cleo's thirds are claims on them (`ben owes me`), due in a week, and each payment carries the month's code (`^rent-2025-03`). A claim that is rent counts as rent when it is paid: what they pay takes it off mine.
2025-03-01 checking            ->   landlord     3_150.00 USD #rent
2025-03-01 ben                 owes me           1_050.00 USD #rent ^rent-2025-03 due 2025-03-08
2025-03-01 cleo                owes me           1_050.00 USD #rent ^rent-2025-03 due 2025-03-08
2025-03-01 checking            =    2_068.44 USD
2025-03-01 savings             =    3_100.00 USD
2025-03-01 wallet              =    240.00 USD
2025-03-01 visa                =    412.66 USD
2025-03-01 collective-checking =    1_842.30 USD
2025-03-01 collective-cash     =    96.50 USD

/// Cash tips, counted on Sunday night: taxable income when received, reported to the employer monthly.
2025-03-02 wallet   <- ?           163.14 USD   #tips
2025-03-02 checking <- ben         1_050.00 USD ^rent-2025-03
2025-03-03 checking -> progressive 128 USD
2025-03-04 checking <- cleo        1_050.00 USD ^rent-2025-03
2025-03-06 wallet   -> ?           8.74 USD     #dining

/// The Lantern: hourly wages plus card tips, paid every second Friday.
2025-03-07 checking <- lantern 1_440.25 USD #wages   // 1_036.00 wages + 404.25 card tips
2025-03-07 checking -> irs     178.59 USD
2025-03-07 checking -> ssa     110.18 USD

/// Shared groceries on my card: split three ways.
2025-03-07 visa   ->   ?           85.05 USD  #groceries
2025-03-07 ben    owes me          28.35 USD  #groceries ^shared-2025-03 due 2025-04-21
2025-03-07 cleo   owes me          28.35 USD  #groceries ^shared-2025-03 due 2025-04-21
2025-03-08 visa   ->   mint-mobile 45 USD
2025-03-09 wallet <-   ?           233.07 USD #tips

/// Internet, 69.99 USD, in my name, split three ways. The month's small bills all carry one code (`^shared-2025-03`): Ben and Cleo pay them at month end with one flow that carries it.
2025-03-09 checking            ->   fiberco 69.99 USD
2025-03-09 ben                 owes me      23.33 USD #utilities ^shared-2025-03 due 2025-04-23
2025-03-09 cleo                owes me      23.33 USD #utilities ^shared-2025-03 due 2025-04-23
2025-03-09 collective-checking <-   ?       60 USD    #donations

/// Electricity is in Ben's name: he pays the bill and I owe him my third (`me owes ben`), a claim of his due in a month. Nothing moves in my bank until I pay it,
/// and the electricity is spending on the day I do. The party is Ben, the one owed, not power-co.
2025-03-12 me       owes ben              29.47 USD  #utilities ^power-2025-03 due 2025-04-11  // my third of 88.40, from power-co
2025-03-12 checking ->   carmax-finance   330.50 USD
2025-03-13 wallet   ->   ?                8.53 USD   #dining
2025-03-14 visa     ->   ?                74.73 USD  #dining
2025-03-15 checking ->   marketplace-plan 189.40 USD

